    "vectorText": "21st Century Integrated Digital Experience Act, website modernization, digital services, executive agency, accessibility, section 508, consistent appearance, search function, secure connection, user needs, data-driven analysis, digital transactions, mobile devices, public-facing applications, digital format, electronic signatures, customer experience, digital service delivery, funding, qualitative data, quantitative data, areas of concern, satisfaction, standardization, interoperability, compliance, Budget request, public reporting, legacy websites, mobile-friendly, non-digital services, paper-based forms, documented processes, physical availability, accessible methods, implementation, Federal Supply Schedule, Technology Transformation Services, information security, digital conversion rates, customer service, modernization, digital forms, digital options, recommendations, coordination, Chief Information Officer, management leaders, cost estimation, future transitions, centralized shared services, GSA, web-based applications, web-based forms, public engagement, digital mediums, data analysis, feedback loops, reporting, prioritization, process improvements, regulatory changes, legislative changes, government services, public access, digital enhancement, digital user experience, legacy system review, executive management, strategic implementation, digital needs assessment, digital service framework, user behaviors, transaction efficiency, digital compliance, system compatibility, design standards, legislative history, stakeholder engagement, online services, government modernization, digital landscape, user-centric design, effective communication, efficiency metrics, government transparency, digital resources, web standards, digital infrastructure, service innovation, application development, future government services, digital engagement strategies, end-user testing, service optimization, technology adoption, user satisfaction, web accessibility, public accountability, service improvement plans, executive oversight, digital policy adherence, government accountability, service effectiveness. ### Summary of Primary Standards, Guidelines, and Requirements 1. **Website Modernization Requirements (New and Redesigned)** - Ensure accessibility for individuals with disabilities (Section 508). - Maintain a consistent appearance across websites. - Prevent overlap or duplication with legacy websites. - Implement an effective search function for users. - Use industry-standard secure connections. - Design based on user needs with data-driven analysis; continuously test. - Offer a customizable digital experience for efficient transactions. - Ensure full functionality on common mobile devices. 2. **Review and Reporting of Existing Websites** - Conduct a review of existing websites/services within one year. - Submit a report to Congress listing top websites and modernization priorities along with cost estimations. 3. **Compliance and Standardization** - New public websites must meet GSA website standards. - Aim for standardization across agencies for shared services. 4. **Digital Services and Forms** - Identify and transition non-digital services to digital formats within 180 days. - Ensure all public forms are available in a digital format within two years. - Document non-digitizable processes and potential solutions. 5. **Electronic Signatures** - Submit a plan to accelerate the use of electronic signatures within 180 days. 6. **Customer Experience Improvement** - Coordinate customer experience programs and strategies. - Monitor and improve digital service delivery based on customer feedback. - Ensure compliance with federal digital service standards. ### Shortened Summary 1. **Website Modernization** - Ensure accessibility, usability, and secure connections. 2. **Website Review** - Review existing sites and report priorities within one year. 3. **Compliance** - Adhere to GSA standards for public websites. 4. **Digital Services** - Shift non-digital services to digital and document issues. 5. **Electronic Signatures** - Develop a plan for electronic signature use. 6. **Customer Experience** - Enhance service delivery based on feedback and ensure compliance."
