    "vectorText": "Managing Customer Experience, Service Delivery, Federal Government Customer, Customer Experience, High-Impact Service Providers (HISPs), Customer Feedback, Digital Service Delivery, Customer Satisfaction, Trust in Government, Human-Centered Design, Equity, Transparency, Efficiency, Measuring Experience, Survey Design, Service Identification, Multi-Channel Services, Customer Journeys, Performance Indicators, Accountability, Annual Performance Plan, Service Quality, Customer Understanding, Governance, Strategy, Service Design, Improvement Actions, Feedback Data, Continuous Improvement, User Testing, Customer Research, Qualitative Research, Quantitative Research, Feedback Mechanisms, Customer Needs, Accessibility, Publicly Available Data, Performance.gov, Annual Capacity Assessment, Action Plan, Priority Life Events, Customer Touchpoints, Service Types, Administrative Services, Benefits, Compliance, Recreation, Informational Services, Data and Research, Regulatory Services, Service Coordination, Customer Interaction, Digital Channels, In-Person Services, Telephonic Services, Postal Services, Measurement Framework, Survey Questions, Response Rates, Data Collection, CX Program Maturity, Service Delivery Improvement, Reporting, Life Experiences, Public Reporting, Performance Improvement, Technology Integration, Collaboration, Customer Segments, Trust Metrics, Aggregate Data, Customer Experience Drivers, Goals, Challenges, Target Dates, Public Feedback, Accountability Mechanisms, Performance Accountability, Public Engagement, Customer-Centric Approach, Feedback Survey Design, Action-Based Feedback, Stakeholder Engagement, Agencies’ Responsibilities, Expectation Management, Outcomes, Operational Measures, User Experience, Administrative Data, Research Methodologies, Service Delivery Challenges, Service Satisfaction. ### Document Summary #### Primary Standards, Guidelines, and Requirements: 1. **Responsibility for Customer Experience**: All Executive agencies must manage customer experience and improve service delivery using leading practices. - *Shorter*: Agencies must enhance customer experience. 2. **Defining Federal Customers**: Customers include individuals, businesses, and organizations interacting with Federal agencies. - *Shorter*: Define customers as various stakeholders. 3. **Understanding Customer Experience**: Customer experience comprises all interactions with Federal agencies, impacting satisfaction and trust. - *Shorter*: Customer experience affects trust and satisfaction. 4. **Service Delivery Definition**: Service delivery includes all customer interactions with agencies to receive public offerings or compliance. - *Shorter*: Service delivery encompasses all customer interactions. 5. **Identifying Services**: Agencies must document their services, including descriptions, responsible units, and delivery channels. - *Shorter*: Document services and delivery channels. 6. **Multiple-Channel Availability**: Services must be available in diverse channels to enhance accessibility and reach all customers. - *Shorter*: Ensure services are multichannel. 7. **Digital Service Delivery**: Agencies should provide services through digital channels while following best practices for customer experience. - *Shorter*: Digital services must follow best practices. 8. **Purpose of Guidance**: Implementing the guidance aims to create a cohesive and accountable approach to customer experience across agencies. - *Shorter*: Establish a consistent approach to customer experience. 9. **Managing Customer Experience**: Agencies need to measure, govern, and improve customer experience continuously. - *Shorter*: Continuous measurement and improvement of customer experience are required. 10. **Customer Feedback Surveys**: Agencies should survey customer experiences to obtain real-time feedback and actionable data. - *Shorter*: Collect immediate customer feedback. 11. **Integration into Annual Plans**: Customer experience measures must be reflected in agency Annual Performance Plans. - *Shorter*: Include customer metrics in performance plans. 12. **Customer Experience Capacity Assessments**: High-Impact Service Providers (HISPs) must assess their customer experience capabilities annually and report findings. - *Shorter*: HISPs must annually assess customer experience. 13. **Feedback Data Submission**: HISPs must submit feedback data to OMB quarterly. - *Shorter*: Quarterly feedback reporting is mandatory. 14. **Action Plans for Improvement**: HISPs should create annual action plans focused on enhancing services based on feedback findings. - *Shorter*: HISPs need annual improvement action plans. #### Focus Areas: - **Security**: Ensure secure methods are employed for service delivery, particularly in digital interactions (implied in guidelines on digital service). - *Shorter*: Implement secure digital services. - **Accessibility**: Services must be accessible through multiple channels to reach all customers, including those marginalized (e.g., traditionally underserved groups). - *Shorter*: Services should be accessible to all customers. - **User Experience**: Customer experience should be a priority, focusing on user-friendly design and effective service delivery. - *Shorter*: Prioritize user-friendly services. - **Compliance**: Adhere to OMB guidelines regarding customer experience and service delivery. - *Shorter*: Follow OMB compliance standards. This summary encapsulates the essential elements of the standards document for non-technical stakeholders, emphasizing key areas of focus that are critical for compliance with government expectations on customer experience."
